1
00:05:06,666 --> 00:05:12,666
The Canterville Ghost is a tv movie, fantasy, drama
film directed by Sydney Macartney.

2
00:10:13,333 --> 00:10:19,333
When a teenaged girl moves to England, with her brothers and parents
into the ancient Canterville Hall, she's not at all happy.

3
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:26,000
Especially as there's a ghost and a mysterious
re-appearing bloodstain on the hearth.

4
00:20:26,666 --> 00:20:32,666
She campaigns to go back home, and her dad, believing the ghost's
pranks are Ginny's, is ready to send her back.

5
00:25:33,333 --> 00:25:39,333
But then Ginny actually meets the elusive 17th-century Sir Simon de Canterville (not to mention the cute
teenaged duke next door), and she sets her hand to the task of freeing Sir Simon from his curse.

6
00:30:40,000 --> 00:30:46,000
Sir Simon de Canterville, played by Patrick Stewart.

7
00:35:46,666 --> 00:35:52,666
Virginia 'Ginny' Otis, played by Neve Campbell.

8
00:40:53,333 --> 00:40:59,333
Mrs. Umney, played by Joan Sims.

9
00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:06,000
Mr. Umney, played by Donald Sinden.

10
00:51:06,666 --> 00:51:12,666
Lucille Otis, played by Cherie Lunghi.

11
00:56:13,333 --> 00:56:19,333
George, Lord Canterville, played by Leslie Phillips.

12
01:01:20,000 --> 01:01:26,000
The Canterville Ghost is a 1996 family film directed by Sydney Macartney.

13
01:06:26,666 --> 01:06:32,666
The mystery, romance, and adventure stars Patrick Stewart and Neve Campbell; it is based on an 1887 Oscar Wilde
short story of the same title which was serialized in the magazine The Court and Society Review.

14
01:11:33,333 --> 01:11:39,333
This story has been adapted to film and made-for-TV movies several
times since the original film of the same name.

15
01:16:40,000 --> 01:16:46,000
Filming was done at Knebworth House in Hertfordshire.

16
01:21:46,666 --> 01:21:52,666
The film explores themes of england, prank, curse, ghost.

17
01:26:53,333 --> 01:26:59,333
The tone is emotional.
